@startuml c4-context
' C4 level 1 — system context.
' CON-008 fixes most of this diagram: every response is HTML for a person in a browser and there is
' no machine-facing API, so nothing consumes this system. Outbound is a separate question - ADR-0008
' leaves a hosted CAPTCHA provider open, and choosing one adds an external system here.
!pragma layout smetana
!include <C4/C4_Context>

title Exchange Student Guide — system context (C4 level 1)

Person(reader, "Reader", "An incoming exchange student looking for an answer. No account (CON-001).")
Person(contributor, "Contributor", "Someone who has just solved a problem and can describe it. No account (CON-001).")
Person(moderator, "OGE moderator", "Staff of the Office of Global Engagement. Not an account either — a shared admin password, ADR-0009.")

System(guide, "Exchange Student Guide", "A community-editable knowledge base. Anyone submits; OGE approves what is published.")

Rel(reader, guide, "Searches, reads, follows links, reports a problem", "HTTPS")
Rel(contributor, guide, "Submits an article or an edit, with an optional file", "HTTPS")
Rel(moderator, guide, "Reviews the queue, approves, rejects, edits, removes", "HTTPS")

note bottom of guide
  No external system is shown because none is
  decided. If ADR-0008 settles on a **hosted**
  CAPTCHA provider, it belongs on this diagram.
end note

SHOW_LEGEND()
@enduml
